    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"strategic investment\" angle is clever, but there's a problem. The internal report explicitly says there is no 18-month federal grant rolling-back program included in the current draft. It's a flat cost requirement for those firms. \n\nIf Miller's team realizes we're talking about a program that doesn't exist in the actual text, it's going to blow up in our faces and ruin our credibility with the committee. Is there a way to pivot the talking point to address the cost without mentioning a recovery program that isn't there? I need something that sounds just as reassuring but is actually defensible if they read the bill word for word.",
